# Git commit message format

When creating any git commit in this project, use this exact structure:

```
<TICKET>
- <what was done 1>
- <what was done 2>
```

## Rules

1. **First line: ticket number only** (example `SHO-3`). No other text on that line.
   - Take the ticket from the chat/dialog title, or from the user stating it at the start of the dialog.
   - If the ticket is unknown, ask before committing.
2. **Then one or more bullet lines** in English: `- <what was done>`.
   - Each bullet is a short, concrete description of a change in the commit.
   - Do not write a prose subject/body paragraph instead of bullets.
3. Apply this format for every new commit and for amend message corrections.

## Example

```
SHO-3
- add Development/Release/persistent Docker Compose run scripts for Messenger Server
- wire companion Postgres secrets into Persistence without host credentials files
```

## Anti-patterns (do not use)

```
- SHO-3 follow-up: describe everything in one sentence.

Adds detailed prose paragraphs instead of ticket + bullets.
```
